## Context

Found during 0416 (PR #760): the pinned snapshot pipeline-2026-06-05.ods
carries a leaked spreadsheet formula error (`Err:510`) in the capacity
column for Vung Ang 2 Unit 1/2. `extract_ods.py`'s validate_input
green-lit it; the failure surfaced only downstream, in
aggregate_units.py's capacity-numericness guard. Per the layered-guards
doctrine (0416 log 2026-06-04T13:35Z): extraction is the PRIMARY catch
for master regressions.

## Quoi faire

1. validate_input in data/reference/extract_ods.py: capacity column
   must parse as a positive number on every unit/plant-grain row;
   spreadsheet error strings (Err:NNN, #VALUE!, #REF!, ...) are named
   explicitly in the diagnostic. Hard stop, no CSV written.
2. Regression test: fixture row with Err:510 -> extraction refuses with
   actionable message naming row and value.
3. Keep redundant with the 0416 aggregate guard (defence in depth) —
   do NOT remove the downstream check.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Extraction refuses non-numeric capacity with actionable message
- [ ] Regression test green
- [ ] `make check` passes

## Related

- 0416 (PR #760 — discovery + downstream guard), 0420 (extraction),
  0439 (master conventions). NOTE: the master itself still needs the
  formula fix + re-import (author, needs-human path documented in
  PR #760).
